Deterministic precedence backfills (filer currency, first-posted ship-to evidence) with no constraint over existing data; readers fail closed on NULL rather than substituting current configuration. The tax_filings backfill must pass the baseline tax_filing_immutable guard, which refuses every UPDATE but prepared->filed: the file suspends that one trigger around the single NULL-guarded UPDATE inside its own transaction and asserts it is enabled again before commit (UPG-0265), so populated installs upgrade and no existing data can make it refuse. The documents ship-to UPDATE changes only the new columns, which no documents guard watches.
